#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Noise, and how to undo it {#3-noise-and-how-to-undo-it}"
msgstr "3. Hingar, dan cara membatalkannya {#3-noise-and-how-to-undo-it}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "A noisy simulation {#a-noisy-simulation}"
msgstr "Simulasi berhingar {#a-noisy-simulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now add noise: 1% two-qubit depolarizing noise on every CZ gate and a 3% readout error on every qubit, sampled with the Qiskit Aer sampler. With 144 CZ gates in the circuit, this is much less noise than the 8×8 hardware circuits see, but enough to see what it does. The simulation uses six couplings and 4,000 shots each, and takes about 1.5 minutes.\n"
"> **Question.** Before you run it: will noise make the system look more thermalized or less thermalized?\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang tambahkan hingar: hingar depolarizing dua-qubit 1% pada setiap gate CZ dan ralat bacaan 3% pada setiap qubit, disampel dengan sampler Qiskit Aer. Dengan 144 gate CZ dalam litar, ini hingar yang jauh lebih sedikit daripada yang dialami litar perkakasan 8×8, tetapi cukup untuk melihat kesannya. Simulasi menggunakan enam gandingan dan 4,000 syot setiap satu, dan mengambil masa kira-kira 1.5 minit.\n"
"> **Soalan.** Sebelum anda menjalankannya: adakah hingar menjadikan sistem kelihatan lebih terterma atau kurang terterma?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "More. Noise scrambles the outcomes, which pushes every marginal distribution toward uniform, so the raw IPR drops and the entropy rises. Without mitigation, noise looks like thermalization that is not there, and the crossovers come out too early.\n"
msgstr "Lebih. Hingar mengacau hasil, yang menolak setiap taburan marginal ke arah seragam, jadi IPR mentah menurun dan entropi meningkat. Tanpa mitigasi, hingar kelihatan seperti pentermaan yang sebenarnya tidak wujud, dan titik persilangan muncul terlalu awal.\n"

