msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/8680e8eb-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Brainstorm: how would you undo this? {#brainstorm-how-would-you-undo-this}"
msgstr "Sumbang saran: bagaimana anda akan membatalkannya? {#brainstorm-how-would-you-undo-this}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Suggested approach\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Pendekatan yang dicadangkan\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At small $J$, the state is barely entangled, so the ideal answer there is cheap to compute classically, even for 64 qubits. That suggests measuring the effect of the noise at a small calibration coupling $J_0$ and correcting every other coupling with it. There are two natural ways to do that, called low-entanglement calibration (LEC):\n"
msgstr "Pada $J$ kecil, keadaan hampir tidak terkusut, jadi jawapan unggul di situ murah untuk dikira secara klasik, walaupun untuk 64 qubit. Itu mencadangkan kita mengukur kesan hingar pada gandingan penentukuran kecil $J_0$ dan membetulkan setiap gandingan lain dengannya. Terdapat dua cara semula jadi untuk melakukannya, dipanggil penentukuran kekusutan rendah (LEC):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**LEC on the IPR.** Rescale the excess of the IPR over its value for a uniform distribution, $2^{-n_A}$, by one factor per marginal:\n"
msgstr "**LEC pada IPR.** Skalakan semula lebihan IPR berbanding nilainya untuk taburan seragam, $2^{-n_A}$, dengan satu faktor bagi setiap marginal:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{LEC}}_A(J) = 2^{-n_A} + R_0\\bigl(\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{raw}}_A(J) - 2^{-n_A}\\bigr), \\qquad R_0 = \\frac{\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{ideal}}_A(J_0) - 2^{-n_A}}{\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{raw}}_A(J_0) - 2^{-n_A}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{LEC}}_A(J) = 2^{-n_A} + R_0\\bigl(\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{raw}}_A(J) - 2^{-n_A}\\bigr), \\qquad R_0 = \\frac{\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{ideal}}_A(J_0) - 2^{-n_A}}{\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{raw}}_A(J_0) - 2^{-n_A}}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**LEC on the $\\langle Z \\rangle$ expectation values.** Rescale every parity of the marginal by its own factor, and rebuild the IPR with the Parseval formula:\n"
msgstr "**LEC pada nilai jangkaan $\\langle Z \\rangle$.** Skalakan semula setiap pariti marginal dengan faktornya sendiri, dan bina semula IPR dengan formula Parseval:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"r_S = \\frac{\\langle Z_S \\rangle^{\\mathrm{ideal}}(J_0)}{\\langle Z_S \\rangle^{\\mathrm{raw}}(J_0)}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{LEC}}_A(J) = 2^{-n_A}\\Bigl(1 + \\sum_{S} r_S^2 \\, \\langle Z_S \\rangle^{\\mathrm{raw}}(J)^2\\Bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"r_S = \\frac{\\langle Z_S \\rangle^{\\mathrm{ideal}}(J_0)}{\\langle Z_S \\rangle^{\\mathrm{raw}}(J_0)}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{LEC}}_A(J) = 2^{-n_A}\\Bigl(1 + \\sum_{S} r_S^2 \\, \\langle Z_S \\rangle^{\\mathrm{raw}}(J)^2\\Bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the code, each squared rescaled parity is debiased by subtracting its variance, as in section 2.\n"
msgstr "Dalam kod, setiap pariti terskala semula yang dikuasa duakan dinyahpincangkan dengan menolak variansnya, seperti dalam bahagian 2.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both are the same if every $r_S^2$ equals $R_0$.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-duanya sama jika setiap $r_S^2$ bersamaan $R_0$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"> **Question.** What are the pros and cons of these methods?\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Pros**\n"
msgstr "**Pros**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Cheap:** no extra data is needed from the device, only a classical simulation at $J_0$.\n"
msgstr "**Murah:** tiada data tambahan diperlukan daripada peranti, hanya simulasi klasik pada $J_0$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Uses the structure of the circuit:** the circuit depth and the CZ layers do not change with $J$, so the noise at $J_0$ is the same noise as at every other $J$.\n"
msgstr "**Menggunakan struktur litar:** kedalaman litar dan lapisan CZ tidak berubah dengan $J$, jadi hingar pada $J_0$ ialah hingar yang sama seperti pada setiap $J$ lain.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Cons**\n"
msgstr "**Cons**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Assumes the effect of the noise on the observables does not depend on $J$:** the noise itself is the same, but how it damps the IPR or each $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ can change as $J$ grows.\n"
msgstr "**Mengandaikan kesan hingar terhadap observable tidak bergantung pada $J$:** hingar itu sendiri sama, tetapi cara ia melemahkan IPR atau setiap $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ boleh berubah apabila $J$ meningkat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both methods on the noisy simulation {#both-methods-on-the-noisy-simulation}"
msgstr "Kedua-dua kaedah pada simulasi berhingar {#both-methods-on-the-noisy-simulation}"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/212cb53d-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/212cb53d-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both methods remove most of the damage: the raw estimates in the previous plot are far too random, and the mitigated ones follow the exact curves. The differences show up for the larger marginals.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua kaedah menghapuskan sebahagian besar kerosakan: anggaran mentah dalam plot sebelumnya terlalu rawak, dan yang telah dimitigasi mengikuti lengkung tepat. Perbezaan muncul pada marginal yang lebih besar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the small marginals both methods work. For the $3 \\times 3$ marginal, LEC on $\\langle Z \\rangle$ is clearly closer.\n"
msgstr "Untuk marginal kecil kedua-dua kaedah berfungsi. Untuk marginal $3 \\times 3$, LEC pada $\\langle Z \\rangle$ jelas lebih hampir.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Why LEC on the IPR gives too little entropy.** Too little entropy means the IPR is too big: LEC on the IPR over-inflates it. It assumes that noise damps the contribution of every $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ to the IPR by the same factor. At $J_0$, every $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ is close to $\\pm 1$, so all strings contribute equally, and most strings have medium weight: of the 511 strings of a $3 \\times 3$ marginal, 252 have weight 4 or 5, and only nine have weight 1. Noise damps a string more the higher its weight (readout error alone damps a weight-$w$ string by $0.94^w$), so the single factor $R_0$ is set mainly by the damping of medium-weight strings. As $J$ grows, the higher-weight $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ decay fastest, and the IPR is carried more and more by low-weight strings, which noise damps less. Boosting them with a factor learned mainly from more heavily damped strings over-inflates the IPR. The effect grows with the size of the marginal, since a larger marginal has a wider range of weights. It is largest at intermediate $J$, after the mix of strings has shifted but while the excess of the IPR over its uniform value still matters.\n"
msgstr "**Mengapa LEC pada IPR memberikan entropi yang terlalu sedikit.** Entropi yang terlalu sedikit bermakna IPR terlalu besar: LEC pada IPR mengembungkannya secara berlebihan. Ia mengandaikan bahawa hingar melemahkan sumbangan setiap $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ kepada IPR dengan faktor yang sama. Pada $J_0$, setiap $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ hampir dengan $\\pm 1$, jadi semua rentetan menyumbang sama rata, dan kebanyakan rentetan mempunyai berat sederhana: daripada 511 rentetan marginal $3 \\times 3$, 252 mempunyai berat 4 atau 5, dan hanya sembilan mempunyai berat 1. Hingar melemahkan rentetan lebih banyak apabila beratnya lebih tinggi (ralat bacaan sahaja melemahkan rentetan berat-$w$ sebanyak $0.94^w$), jadi faktor tunggal $R_0$ ditentukan terutamanya oleh pelemahan rentetan berat sederhana. Apabila $J$ meningkat, $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ berat lebih tinggi mereput paling cepat, dan IPR semakin banyak dibawa oleh rentetan berat rendah, yang kurang dilemahkan oleh hingar. Menggandakan mereka dengan faktor yang dipelajari terutamanya daripada rentetan yang lebih banyak dilemahkan akan mengembungkan IPR secara berlebihan. Kesannya bertambah dengan saiz marginal, kerana marginal yang lebih besar mempunyai julat berat yang lebih luas. Ia paling besar pada $J$ pertengahan, selepas campuran rentetan telah beralih tetapi ketika lebihan IPR berbanding nilai seragamnya masih penting.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Why LEC on $\\langle Z \\rangle$ errs the other way.** It rescales each string by its own factor, so the shift between weights does not affect it. It only assumes that each string keeps its $J_0$ damping. As $J$ grows, each $Z_S$ spreads into higher-weight operators, which pick up more noise than at $J_0$, so the factors slightly under-correct and the entropy comes out slightly too high.\n"
msgstr "**Mengapa LEC pada $\\langle Z \\rangle$ tersasar ke arah lain.** Ia menskalakan semula setiap rentetan dengan faktornya sendiri, jadi peralihan antara berat tidak menjejaskannya. Ia hanya mengandaikan bahawa setiap rentetan mengekalkan pelemahan $J_0$nya. Apabila $J$ meningkat, setiap $Z_S$ merebak ke dalam operator berat lebih tinggi, yang menerima lebih banyak hingar berbanding pada $J_0$, jadi faktor itu membetulkan sedikit kurang dan entropi menjadi sedikit terlalu tinggi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So the prediction to test on hardware is: **the larger the marginal, the more LEC on $\\langle Z \\rangle$ should win**. On hardware, the noise is stronger and not of a known form.\n"
msgstr "Jadi ramalan untuk diuji pada perkakasan ialah: **semakin besar marginal, semakin LEC pada $\\langle Z \\rangle$ patut menang**. Pada perkakasan, hingar lebih kuat dan bukan daripada bentuk yang diketahui.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Run at scale {#4-run-at-scale}"
msgstr "4. Jalankan pada skala besar {#4-run-at-scale}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The hardware experiment runs an $8 \\times 8$ lattice with four cycles: 64 qubits and 1,344 CZ gates in 48 layers, at nine couplings. Five things change compared with the simulation:\n"
msgstr "Eksperimen perkakasan menjalankan kekisi $8 \\times 8$ dengan empat kitaran: 64 qubit dan 1,344 gate CZ dalam 48 lapisan, pada sembilan gandingan. Lima perkara berubah berbanding simulasi:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The noise has to be **learned**, which only works if the CZ layers are fixed.\n"
msgstr "Hingar perlu **dipelajari**, yang hanya berfungsi jika lapisan CZ ditetapkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Twirling** turns the noise of each layer into a Pauli channel, which can be learned and amplified.\n"
msgstr "**Twirling** menukar hingar setiap lapisan kepada saluran Pauli, yang boleh dipelajari dan diamplifikasikan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Dynamical decoupling (DD)** protects idle qubits.\n"
msgstr "**Dynamical decoupling (DD)** melindungi qubit yang melahu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Noise amplification** for PEA runs in the same job as the main data.\n"
msgstr "**Amplifikasi hingar** untuk PEA dijalankan dalam kerja yang sama dengan data utama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**MPS simulations** at small $J$ provide the classical references for LEC-based error mitigation.\n"
msgstr "**Simulasi MPS** pada $J$ kecil menyediakan rujukan klasik untuk mitigasi ralat berasaskan LEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The cells that need a backend only run when `RUN_ON_HARDWARE` is `True`. MPS simulations can be rerun with `COMPUTE_MPS_REFERENCES` set to `True`. The other cells run here.\n"
msgstr "Sel yang memerlukan backend hanya dijalankan apabila `RUN_ON_HARDWARE` ialah `True`. Simulasi MPS boleh dijalankan semula dengan `COMPUTE_MPS_REFERENCES` ditetapkan kepada `True`. Sel lain dijalankan di sini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fixed CZ layers {#fixed-cz-layers}"
msgstr "Lapisan CZ tetap {#fixed-cz-layers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Boxes for noise learning {#boxes-for-noise-learning}"
msgstr "Kotak untuk pembelajaran hingar {#boxes-for-noise-learning}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Samplomatic boxing pass manager then groups each circuit into *boxes*: one per CZ layer and one for the measurements. Each box carries a reference to the noise model it needs, so you can check that all couplings share the same boxes. The next cell does this for the $8 \\times 8$ circuits of the hardware run, compiled to CZ gates without a backend, and prints the boxes that noise learning will characterize.\n"
msgstr "Pengurus laluan boxing Samplomatic kemudian mengumpulkan setiap litar ke dalam *kotak*: satu bagi setiap lapisan CZ dan satu untuk pengukuran. Setiap kotak membawa rujukan kepada model hingar yang diperlukannya, jadi anda boleh menyemak bahawa semua gandingan berkongsi kotak yang sama. Sel seterusnya melakukan ini untuk litar $8 \\times 8$ bagi larian perkakasan, dikompil kepada gate CZ tanpa backend, dan mencetak kotak yang akan dicirikan oleh pembelajaran hingar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twirl the circuits {#twirl-the-circuits}"
msgstr "Pusingkan litar {#twirl-the-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In every randomization, Samplomatic puts random Pauli gates before each box and the compensating gates after it, merged into the neighboring single-qubit gates. Averaged over randomizations, the noise of each layer becomes a Pauli channel, which `NoiseLearnerV3` can learn as a sparse Pauli-Lindblad model and the PEA step can amplify. Measurement twirling randomly flips bits before readout. The flips are undone in software, which makes the readout noise symmetric and is the basis of the readout correction (TREX).\n"
msgstr "Dalam setiap rawakan, Samplomatic meletakkan gate Pauli rawak sebelum setiap kotak dan gate pampasan selepasnya, digabungkan ke dalam gate satu-qubit bersebelahan. Dipuratakan ke atas rawakan, hingar setiap lapisan menjadi saluran Pauli, yang boleh dipelajari oleh `NoiseLearnerV3` sebagai model Pauli-Lindblad jarang dan diamplifikasikan oleh langkah PEA. Twirling pengukuran membalikkan bit secara rawak sebelum bacaan. Pembalikan itu dibatalkan dalam perisian, yang menjadikan hingar bacaan simetri dan merupakan asas pembetulan bacaan (TREX).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The hardware workflow {#the-hardware-workflow}"
msgstr "Aliran kerja perkakasan {#the-hardware-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose the qubits, compile the circuits, then learn the noise and run the sweep. These cells are switched off here.\n"
msgstr "Pilih qubit, kompil litar, kemudian pelajari hingar dan jalankan sapuan. Sel ini dimatikan di sini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Choose the qubits.** Nighthawk's square grid holds the $8 \\times 8$ lattice without SWAP gates. The cell scores every $8 \\times 8$ rectangle of the grid by its reported CZ and readout errors and takes the best.\n"
msgstr "**Pilih qubit.** Grid segi empat Nighthawk memuatkan kekisi $8 \\times 8$ tanpa gate SWAP. Sel ini menilai setiap segi empat tepat $8 \\times 8$ pada grid mengikut ralat CZ dan bacaan yang dilaporkan dan memilih yang terbaik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Compile.** The same steps as above on the chosen qubits, followed by `build`, which turns each boxed circuit into a template circuit and a *samplex*, the recipe for drawing the twirling gates and the injected noise. DD is added to the templates.\n"
msgstr "**Kompil.** Langkah yang sama seperti di atas pada qubit yang dipilih, diikuti oleh `build`, yang menukar setiap litar berkotak kepada litar templat dan *samplex*, resipi untuk melukis gate twirling dan hingar yang disuntik. DD ditambah pada templat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Learn the noise and run the sweep.** One `NoiseLearnerV3` job learns all five boxes: a Pauli-Lindblad model for each of the four CZ layers, and the readout noise of the measurement box. Then one `QuantumProgram` holds all nine couplings. Each item gets its template, its samplex, the learned noise models, and three noise scales. A scale of 0 is the unamplified data for both LEC methods. Scales of 0.5 and 1 add 50% and 100% of the learned noise for PEA, which extrapolates back to zero noise. This uses about 40 seconds of QPU time.\n"
msgstr "**Pelajari hingar dan jalankan sapuan.** Satu kerja `NoiseLearnerV3` mempelajari kesemua lima kotak: model Pauli-Lindblad bagi setiap satu daripada empat lapisan CZ, dan hingar bacaan bagi kotak pengukuran. Kemudian satu `QuantumProgram` memegang kesemua sembilan gandingan. Setiap item mendapat templatnya, samplexnya, model hingar yang dipelajari, dan tiga skala hingar. Skala 0 ialah data tanpa amplifikasi untuk kedua-dua kaedah LEC. Skala 0.5 dan 1 menambah 50% dan 100% hingar yang dipelajari untuk PEA, yang mengekstrapolasi kembali kepada hingar sifar. Ini menggunakan kira-kira 40 saat masa QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. The hardware data {#5-the-hardware-data}"
msgstr "5. Data perkakasan {#5-the-hardware-data}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This section explores how the previous methods perform on real hardware data from a Nighthawk processor.\n"
msgstr "Bahagian ini meneroka prestasi kaedah sebelumnya pada data perkakasan sebenar daripada pemproses Nighthawk.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Load the run {#load-the-run}"
msgstr "Muatkan larian {#load-the-run}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With `RUN_ON_HARDWARE` set to `True`, the next cell converts the results of the two jobs from section 4 and saves them to `data/hardware_run_new.npz`, in the same format as the saved run, so the new run can be analyzed again later. Otherwise it loads the saved run from `data/hardware_run.npz`. The bits are packed along the qubit axis to save space.\n"
msgstr "Dengan `RUN_ON_HARDWARE` ditetapkan kepada `True`, sel seterusnya menukar keputusan kedua-dua kerja daripada bahagian 4 dan menyimpannya ke `data/hardware_run_new.npz`, dalam format yang sama seperti larian yang disimpan, supaya larian baharu boleh dianalisis semula kemudian. Jika tidak, ia memuatkan larian yang disimpan daripada `data/hardware_run.npz`. Bit dipadatkan sepanjang paksi qubit untuk menjimatkan ruang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the kernel restarts while the jobs run, do not submit them again. Rerun the cells before the last call in section 4, check that the same qubits are chosen, and set `learner_job` and `executor_job` to `service.job(job_id)` with the job IDs that were printed out in section 4.\n"
msgstr "Jika kernel dimulakan semula semasa kerja berjalan, jangan hantar semula kerja tersebut. Jalankan semula sel sebelum panggilan terakhir dalam bahagian 4, semak bahawa qubit yang sama dipilih, dan tetapkan `learner_job` dan `executor_job` kepada `service.job(job_id)` dengan ID kerja yang dicetak dalam bahagian 4.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classical references {#classical-references}"
msgstr "Rujukan klasik {#classical-references}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both LEC methods need the ideal marginal distributions at $J_0 = 0.005\\pi$, and testing them needs ideal values at the held-out couplings $J = 0.01\\pi$ and $0.02\\pi$. These come from matrix product state (MPS) simulations, saved for every placement of each marginal shape on the lattice, as in the paper, and for every non-overlapping $2 \\times 2$ block at $J_0$. At $J_0$ they converge at bond dimension $\\chi = 64$. At $J = 0.01\\pi$ and $0.02\\pi$ they use $\\chi = 128$, and at $0.02\\pi$ they still change by up to about 13% from $\\chi = 64$ for $3 \\times 3$ marginals, so treat them as approximate there. The next cell computes them if `COMPUTE_MPS_REFERENCES` is `True`, which takes about 18 minutes, and otherwise loads the saved results, keyed by coupling index, bond dimension, and marginal.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua kaedah LEC memerlukan taburan marginal unggul pada $J_0 = 0.005\\pi$, dan menguji kaedah tersebut memerlukan nilai unggul pada gandingan ketepi $J = 0.01\\pi$ dan $0.02\\pi$. Ini datang daripada simulasi keadaan hasil darab matriks (MPS), disimpan bagi setiap penempatan setiap bentuk marginal pada kekisi, seperti dalam kertas kerja, dan bagi setiap blok $2 \\times 2$ yang tidak bertindih pada $J_0$. Pada $J_0$ ia menumpu pada dimensi ikatan $\\chi = 64$. Pada $J = 0.01\\pi$ dan $0.02\\pi$ ia menggunakan $\\chi = 128$, dan pada $0.02\\pi$ ia masih berubah sehingga kira-kira 13% daripada $\\chi = 64$ untuk marginal $3 \\times 3$, jadi anggaplah ia hampiran di situ. Sel seterusnya mengiranya jika `COMPUTE_MPS_REFERENCES` ialah `True`, yang mengambil masa kira-kira 18 minit, dan jika tidak memuatkan keputusan yang disimpan, dikunci mengikut indeks gandingan, dimensi ikatan, dan marginal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Data quality: faulty couplers / qubits {#data-quality-faulty-couplers--qubits}"
msgstr "Kualiti data: pengganding / qubit yang rosak {#data-quality-faulty-couplers--qubits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, look at the lowest coupling, $J_0$, where the expectation values should be close to the Néel checkerboard.\n"
msgstr "Pertama, lihat gandingan terendah, $J_0$, yang mana nilai jangkaan sepatutnya hampir dengan papan dam Néel.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/48d2dbbb-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/48d2dbbb-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> **Question.** Looking at the hardware map, what stands out?\n"
msgstr "> **Soalan.** Melihat peta perkakasan, apakah yang menonjol?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The pale sites, which have lost almost all of their signal although the state at $J_0$ is close to the Néel state. They matter because LEC divides by whatever signal survives at $J_0$: a qubit with almost no signal gives a huge, noisy correction factor, and a few such qubits can dominate every marginal that contains them.\n"
msgstr "Tapak yang pucat, yang telah kehilangan hampir semua isyaratnya walaupun keadaan pada $J_0$ hampir dengan keadaan Néel. Ia penting kerana LEC membahagi dengan apa-apa isyarat yang tinggal pada $J_0$: qubit yang hampir tiada isyarat memberikan faktor pembetulan yang sangat besar dan berhingar, dan beberapa qubit sedemikian boleh mendominasi setiap marginal yang mengandunginya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A rule that uses only the data: A qubit is faulty if its single-qubit IPR at $J_0$ is within $0.25^2/2 \\approx 0.03$ of $1/2$, the value for a fully mixed qubit. Since the IPR of one qubit is $(1 + \\langle Z \\rangle^2)/2$, this flags qubits with $|\\langle Z \\rangle| < 0.25$. Marginals that contain a flagged site are left out below.\n"
msgstr "Peraturan yang hanya menggunakan data: Sesebuah qubit rosak jika IPR satu-qubitnya pada $J_0$ berada dalam lingkungan $0.25^2/2 \\approx 0.03$ daripada $1/2$, nilai bagi qubit tercampur sepenuhnya. Oleh kerana IPR satu qubit ialah $(1 + \\langle Z \\rangle^2)/2$, ini menandakan qubit dengan $|\\langle Z \\rangle| < 0.25$. Marginal yang mengandungi tapak yang ditandakan dikecualikan di bawah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Select the marginals to average {#select-the-marginals-to-average}"
msgstr "Pilih marginal untuk dipuratakan {#select-the-marginals-to-average}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The next cell shows which placements of each shape enter the averages below: every placement in the bulk of the lattice without a flagged site (red crosses). Placements that touch the edge (shaded) are left out. Edge qubits have fewer bonds, so they scramble more slowly. Averaged on their own, they cross over a full step of $J$ later than bulk placements, for every shape and method. Each averaged placement has its own box, colored by placement.\n"
msgstr "Sel seterusnya menunjukkan penempatan setiap bentuk yang masuk ke dalam purata di bawah: setiap penempatan di bahagian pukal kekisi tanpa tapak yang ditandakan (pangkah merah). Penempatan yang menyentuh tepi (berlorek) dikecualikan. Qubit tepi mempunyai lebih sedikit ikatan, jadi ia mengacau dengan lebih perlahan. Dipuratakan secara berasingan, ia bersilang satu langkah penuh $J$ lebih lewat daripada penempatan pukal, untuk setiap bentuk dan kaedah. Setiap penempatan yang dipuratakan mempunyai kotaknya sendiri, diwarnakan mengikut penempatan.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/d31b217b-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/d31b217b-0.avif)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEA {#pea}"
msgstr "PEA {#pea}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The third method needs no classical reference. For each parity, take the values at noise factors 1, 1.5, and 2, divide out the learned readout damping (TREX), fit an exponential in the noise factor, and extrapolate to zero noise. Parities that change sign or are nearly zero get a straight-line fit. Subtracting the variance needs a reliable estimate of it, which is easy for raw and rescaled parities but not for the output of a nonlinear fit with clipping and fallbacks. PEA therefore uses the other standard way to remove the bias of a square. Extrapolate each half of the randomizations separately and multiply the two independent estimates.\n"
msgstr "Kaedah ketiga tidak memerlukan rujukan klasik. Bagi setiap pariti, ambil nilai pada faktor hingar 1, 1.5, dan 2, bahagikan keluar pelemahan bacaan yang dipelajari (TREX), padankan eksponen dalam faktor hingar, dan ekstrapolasi kepada hingar sifar. Pariti yang bertukar tanda atau hampir sifar mendapat padanan garis lurus. Menolak varians memerlukan anggaran yang boleh dipercayai bagi varians itu, yang mudah untuk pariti mentah dan terskala semula tetapi tidak untuk output padanan tak linear dengan keratan dan sandaran. Oleh itu PEA menggunakan cara piawai lain untuk menghapuskan pincang sesuatu kuasa dua. Ekstrapolasi setiap separuh rawakan secara berasingan dan darabkan kedua-dua anggaran bebas itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "All four estimates, and the crossovers {#all-four-estimates-and-the-crossovers}"
msgstr "Kesemua empat anggaran, dan titik persilangan {#all-four-estimates-and-the-crossovers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The next function computes the raw, LEC-on-IPR, LEC-on-$\\langle Z \\rangle$, and PEA estimates of the IPR of one marginal position at every coupling. It also estimates the shot noise of each, by bootstrapping the randomizations. The cell runs it for every placement that enters the averages, which takes about a minute and a half.\n"
msgstr "Fungsi seterusnya mengira anggaran mentah, LEC-pada-IPR, LEC-pada-$\\langle Z \\rangle$, dan PEA bagi IPR satu kedudukan marginal pada setiap gandingan. Ia juga menganggar hingar syot bagi setiap satu, dengan bootstrap rawakan. Sel ini menjalankannya untuk setiap penempatan yang masuk ke dalam purata, yang mengambil masa kira-kira satu setengah minit.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/6303dec9-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/6303dec9-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Wrap-up {#wrap-up}"
msgstr "Rumusan {#wrap-up}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What it took to run an experiment of this size:\n"
msgstr "Apa yang diperlukan untuk menjalankan eksperimen bersaiz ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Circuits whose structure does not depend on $J$**, compiled one sublayer at a time, so one noise model serves the whole sweep.\n"
msgstr "**Litar yang strukturnya tidak bergantung pada $J$**, dikompil satu sublapisan pada satu masa, supaya satu model hingar melayani keseluruhan sapuan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Estimators that work from bitstrings**: pair counting for the IPR of a marginal, and the Parseval form, with the variance subtracted from each squared parity, when the inputs are mitigated expectation values.\n"
msgstr "**Penganggar yang berfungsi daripada rentetan bit**: pengiraan pasangan untuk IPR sesuatu marginal, dan bentuk Parseval, dengan varians ditolak daripada setiap pariti yang dikuasa duakan, apabila input ialah nilai jangkaan yang dimitigasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A cheap classical anchor**: the ideal state at small $J$ calibrates the noise, and held-out couplings test the calibration. Calibrating each $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ separately, rather than the IPR as a whole, is what makes the large marginals agree.\n"
msgstr "**Sauh klasik yang murah**: keadaan unggul pada $J$ kecil menentukur hingar, dan gandingan ketepi menguji penentukuran itu. Menentukur setiap $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ secara berasingan, dan bukan IPR secara keseluruhan, itulah yang menjadikan marginal besar sepadan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**IBM tools for the heavy lifting**: Samplomatic boxes and twirling, `NoiseLearnerV3`, dynamical decoupling, and one `Executor` job with noise amplification for PEA.\n"
msgstr "**Alat IBM untuk kerja berat**: kotak dan twirling Samplomatic, `NoiseLearnerV3`, dynamical decoupling, dan satu kerja `Executor` dengan amplifikasi hingar untuk PEA.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Data-quality checks** that use only the data.\n"
msgstr "**Semakan kualiti data** yang hanya menggunakan data.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Next steps.** To go further with mitigation, see the [probabilistic error amplification](/tutorials/probabilistic-error-amplification) and [PEC with shaded lightcones](/tutorials/pec-with-shaded-lightcones) tutorials.\n"
msgstr "**Langkah seterusnya.** Untuk meneruskan dengan mitigasi, lihat tutorial [amplifikasi ralat kebarangkalian](/tutorials/probabilistic-error-amplification) dan [PEC dengan kon cahaya berlorek](/tutorials/pec-with-shaded-lightcones).\n"

